{"recall":{"defs":[["Regression","Supervised prediction of a continuous value."],["Linear regression","Output is a linear combination of features plus bias."],["Design matrix X","N × (d+1) table of examples with a leading 1."],["Identity activation","f(z) = z, f′(z) = 1."],["MSE objective","J(w) = (1/2N)‖Xw − y‖²."],["Learning rate η","Gradient-descent step size."],["R²","1 − SS_res/SS_tot."]],"formulas":["\\hat{\\mathbf y}=X\\mathbf w","J(\\mathbf w)=\\frac1{2N}\\|X\\mathbf w-\\mathbf y\\|^2","\\nabla J(\\mathbf w)=\\frac1NX^T(X\\mathbf w-\\mathbf y)","\\mathbf w^{(t+1)}=\\mathbf w^{(t)}-\\frac{\\eta}{N}X^T(X\\mathbf w^{(t)}-\\mathbf y)","\\text{RMSE}=\\sqrt{\\tfrac1N\\sum(\\hat y-y)^2},\\ \\ \\text{MAE}=\\tfrac1N\\sum|y-\\hat y|","R^2=1-SS_{res}/SS_{tot}","x'_j=(x_j-\\mu_j)/\\sigma_j"],"takeaways":["Linear regression = one neuron with identity activation.","Squared error is convex: one global minimum.","Gradient = average of error × input.","η too large diverges, too small crawls; scale features.","Judge generalisation on a test set (MSE, RMSE, MAE, R²)."],"confused":[["J vs MSE","J = MSE/2 (the ½ simplifies the gradient)."],["MSE vs MAE","Squared (outlier-sensitive) vs absolute errors."],["Min–max vs standardisation","Rescale to [0,1] vs zero mean, unit variance."],["Training vs test error","Fit quality vs generalisation."]],"minute":"Linear regression predicts a continuous target as ŷ = w₀ + w₁x₁ + … + w_dx_d. Stacking examples into a design matrix X with a leading column of ones gives ŷ = Xw: a single neuron with identity activation. The objective is J(w) = (1/2N)‖Xw − y‖², which is convex and corresponds to maximum likelihood under Gaussian noise. Its gradient is (1/N)Xᵀ(Xw − y), and batch gradient descent repeats w ← w − η∇J until the gradient is small. In the worked example (x = 1, 2, 3; y = 2, 4, 5; η = 0.1) one step takes w from (0, 0) to (0.367, 0.833) and J from 7.5 to 1.51. Choose η by plotting loss curves, standardise features, stop on small gradients or rising validation loss, and evaluate on a test set with MSE, RMSE, MAE and R²."},"flashcards":[["Regression","Supervised task predicting a continuous value, f: ℝᵈ → ℝ"],["Linear regression equation (1)","$y=w_0+w_1x_1+\\cdots+w_dx_d$"],["Design matrix shape","$X\\in\\mathbb R^{N\\times(d+1)}$ with a leading column of 1s"],["Vectorised prediction (3)","$\\hat{\\mathbf y}=X\\mathbf w$"],["Identity activation","$f(z)=z$, $f'(z)=1$"],["Total loss (6)","$J(\\mathbf w)=\\frac1N\\sum\\frac12(\\mathbf w^T\\mathbf x^{(i)}-y^{(i)})^2$"],["Why squared error","Differentiable, convex, penalises large errors, Gaussian MLE"],["Gradient (10)","$\\nabla J=\\frac1NX^T(X\\mathbf w-\\mathbf y)$"],["Update rule (11)","$\\mathbf w\\leftarrow\\mathbf w-\\frac{\\eta}{N}X^T(X\\mathbf w-\\mathbf y)$"],["Example: initial loss","J(0) = (4 + 16 + 25)/6 = 7.5"],["Example: first gradient","(−3.67, −8.33)"],["Example: w after one step (η = 0.1)","(0.367, 0.833), J = 1.51"],["RMSE","$\\sqrt{\\text{MSE}}$, same units as the target"],["R² interpretation","1 perfect; 0 = mean baseline; < 0 worse than the mean"],["Learning-rate grid to try","{0.001, 0.01, 0.1, 1.0}"],["Standardisation","$x'_j=(x_j-\\mu_j)/\\sigma_j$"]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["what","why"],"deep":["n3-reg","n3-regex","n3-lin","n3-linex"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h1"],"deep":["n3-four","n3-matrix"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2"],"deep":["n3-neuron","n3-identity"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h3"],"deep":["n3-loss","n3-whysq"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4","h5"],"deep":["n3-algo","n3-grad","n3-update"],"viz":["lrRace"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h6","demo"],"deep":["n3-exsetup","n3-exinit","n3-exgrad","n3-exupdate","n3-exloss","n3-graph"],"viz":["gdWorked"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h7"],"deep":["n3-traintest","n3-metrics","n3-r2"],"viz":["metricsLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h8","h9"],"deep":["n3-tips","n3-tips2","n3-debug"],"viz":["scalingRa